claimed: deploy-cli-spec -- operator ask 2026-09-07: a simple CLI in okay-deploy for these purposes. The design decision it forces: the CLI must read the deployment as DATA, so `render` writes deployment.json (the value through its Schema) beside the target's files, and every later verb -- doctor, up, down, diff -- reads that instead of evaluating Scala. Which also means the CLI works on a server that has no repository and no sbt: copy deploy/, run it. Shipped as a fat jar plus a small wrapper script (a JRE is the one prerequisite, and the doctor names it); a Scala Native binary with no JRE at all is filed rather than promised. Named `okay` with `deploy` as the first subcommand group, since okay-script's Serve and okay-acme's Revoke are the same kind of operator-facing main and can join later. Spec only.
